mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Donation Platform API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis backend powers a public donation website supporting two relief causes: Nepal earthquake relief (people who lost homes and relatives) and Africa water, food and medicine. Visitors worldwide can browse published causes and donate online with a card via Stripe. The site owner manages causes and reads the full donation ledger.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nSign-in uses Internet Identity. The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRegistration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. The first authenticated caller to sign in becomes the site owner (admin); subsequent callers receive the user role. A direct API caller must sign in once through the frontend before any owner-guarded call, including guarded queries.\n\n## Authorization\n\n- Public reads and the donation flow are open to signed-out visitors: `listCauses`, `getCause`, `listRecentDonations`, `startDonation`, `confirmDonation`.\n- Owner-only (admin role): `createCause`, `editCause`, `setCauseGoal`, `publishCause`, `closeCause`, `listAllCauses`, `listDonationLedger`.\n- An unregistered or anonymous caller on a guarded endpoint receives a trap: `Unauthorized: Only the site owner can <action>`.\n- Stripe configuration endpoints (`isStripeConfigured`, `setStripeConfiguration`, `createCheckoutSession`, `getStripeSessionStatus`) are provided by the Stripe mixin; `setStripeConfiguration` is admin-guarded.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- All monetary amounts are integer cents (`Nat`) in USD. `goalCents` and `raisedCents` are cents; `amountCents` is cents.\n- `progressBps` is progress in basis points (0..10000); it is 0 when `goalCents` is 0.\n- `createdAt` is signed nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Int`, from `Time.now()`).\n- `donorName` and `message` are optional (`?Text`); a null `donorName` is presented as `Anonymous` in `donorDisplayName`.\n- `receiptRef` is the Stripe checkout session id used as the receipt reference. When no Stripe secret key is configured it is a local reference of the form `local-<donationId>`.\n- `status` variants: cause `#draft | #published | #closed`; donation `#pending | #completed | #failed`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n1. `startDonation` records a pending donation and returns `{ donationId; sessionJson }`. The frontend parses `sessionJson` and redirects to the `url` it carries.\n2. When a Stripe secret key is configured, `sessionJson` is the Stripe checkout session and `url` is the Stripe checkout page. When no key is configured, `sessionJson` is a local session whose `url` is the caller-supplied `successUrl`, so the visitor still reaches the app's own payment step in a fresh draft.\n3. After payment, the frontend calls `confirmDonation(donationId)`. With a key configured this queries Stripe for the session status; on `#completed` the donation is marked completed and the cause `raisedCents` increases by `amountCents`. With no key configured there is no gateway to verify against, so the pending donation is recorded as completed and the cause total increases.\n4. `confirmDonation` is safe to poll: a donation already `#completed` returns its view immediately without re-querying Stripe or double-counting the amount.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `confirmDonation` is idempotent for completed donations: repeated calls return the same view and never add the amount twice.\n- `startDonation` is not idempotent: each call creates a new pending donation and a new checkout session. Retrying after a failure creates a separate donation record.\n- `createCause` always allocates a new id; retrying creates a duplicate draft.\n- `editCause`, `setCauseGoal`, `publishCause`, `closeCause` are idempotent setters.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- `startDonation` traps with `Cause not found`, `Cause is not accepting donations` (cause not published), or `Donation amount must be greater than zero`. It does not trap when Stripe is unconfigured.\n- `confirmDonation` traps with `Donation not found`, or `Payment not completed: <error>` when a configured Stripe session failed. It does not trap when Stripe is unconfigured.\n- Stripe does not need to be configured for a visitor to start and confirm a donation; a saved key only upgrades the flow to a real Stripe checkout session.\n- `listRecentDonations` returns only completed donations, newest first, capped at `limit`.\n- `listDonationLedger` returns every donation for a cause (all statuses), newest first, and is owner-only.\n- `listCauses` returns only published causes; `listAllCauses` (owner-only) returns all statuses.\n";
  };
};
